; Allow containers to connect to the host seatd socket for DRM/KMS access.
;
; This is host-wide on container_t (seatd runs as unconfined_service_t and
; exposes its socket under var_run_t), and its consumers — KMS desktops — are
; bare containers, not workloadctl workloads, so they can't get a per-workload
; type. To avoid leaking the grant to every container all the time, it is gated
; behind a boolean that is OFF by default. Turn it on only while running a KMS
; desktop:
;
;     sudo setsebool -P seatd_container_connect on    # before
;     sudo setsebool -P seatd_container_connect off   # after
;
; A KMS desktop needs the input half too — see container_input_devices.cil,
; which is the same shape and flipped by the same step.
;
(boolean seatd_container_connect false)
(booleanif seatd_container_connect
    (true
        (allow container_t unconfined_service_t (unix_stream_socket (connectto)))
        (allow container_t var_run_t (sock_file (read write getattr)))))
